---
import { heroWork } from '../data/works';
const oc = heroWork.onchain!;
---
<section id="pioneer" class="pioneer" aria-labelledby="pioneer-h">
  <div class="wrap pioneer__grid">
    <div class="pioneer__art">
      <figure class="pioneer__anaglyph">
        <img
          src={heroWork.anaglyphImage}
          alt={heroWork.anaglyphAlt}
          width="2000"
          height="1605"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption class="pioneer__glasses">
          <span class="pioneer__glasses-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          Grab your red/blue 3D glasses
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p class="pioneer__receipt small">
        <span class="pioneer__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        Minted <time datetime="2018-05-07">{oc.minted}</time> · {oc.platform} · {oc.chain} ·
        {oc.url ? <a href={oc.url}>view on-chain</a> : <span class="muted">on-chain record [link to add]</span>}
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="pioneer__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">On-chain since 2018</p>
      <h2 id="pioneer-h">The first stereoscopic artwork on a blockchain.</h2>
      <p>
        On May 7, 2018, Coldie minted <em>{heroWork.title}</em> — the first stereoscopic artwork
        recorded on a blockchain. There was no collector market for it yet; that was the point. He made it
        to prove that peer-to-peer ownership of digital art was real, and that it pointed to the future of
        the digital economy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tokenized on Ethereum through R.A.R.E. Art Labs, it was a bet that if artists tested the technology
        early, names like Shepard Fairey and Banksy would eventually follow. <strong>Fairey has.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="muted small">
        The work you see at the top of this page is this one, in motion. Here it is explained: true 3D,
        the receipt, and the story. The astronaut ascends toward the moon beneath a HODL billboard — hold
        on for dear life — over the artist’s own photographs of Los Angeles and San Francisco, the two
        cities that shaped his twenties and thirties.
      </p>
      <a class="link-arrow" href={`/work/${heroWork.slug}`}>Full wall text & provenance</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .pioneer { padding-block: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 9rem); border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .pioneer__anaglyph { margin: 0; }
  .pioneer__anaglyph img {
    width: 100%; height: auto; /* natural ratio — show the entire artwork, no crop */
    border-radius: var(--radius); background: #05070a;
    display: block;
  }
  .pioneer__glasses {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.55em;
    margin-top: 0.9em;
    font-family: var(--type, var(--sans));
    font-size: 0.82rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .pioneer__glasses-icon {
    width: 26px; height: 13px; border-radius: 2px; flex: none;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e23b2e 0 50%, #45c7d0 50% 100%);
  }
  .pioneer__grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: center;
  }
  .pioneer__receipt {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5em; flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 1.2em; color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .pioneer__dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent-cyan); }
  /* typewriter (top-UI) face for this headline */
  .pioneer__copy h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6em;
    font-family: var(--type);
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .pioneer__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
